720 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 374 0 R
/E (During the visit to the Courtyard Portland Airport, Mr. Griffo sat for an interview. During the interaction, he tended to be concerned with integrating Artificial Intelligence. This was mainly attributed to the regard of Artificial Intelligence disrupting the human touch that has been cultivated ever since hotels were established. He also alluded to self-check-in lanes that many were using. In his belief, these technologies may bring reduced hiring and less need for employees. In terms of where AI usage could be enhanced, Griffo stated that AI could help in sections such as the inventory and the use of products. However, Mr. Griffo did point to how there would be challenges in making staff transfer over to these systems, given how people are not prone to change with technology.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
721 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 374 0 R
/E (Later in the week, when Mr. Beach was reached out too. It was discoved that A1 Hospitality has many systems managing various company operations, such as payroll and accounting. Beyond these systems, A1 Hospitality has revenue management handled by 3rd party companies. Regarding Artificial Intelligence, Mr. Beach sees much more opportunity with the technology, given its ability to cultivate much data in a matter of seconds, which he believes is beneficial to areas of the business such as marketing and revenue management. With regard to challenges facing the company. Mr. Beach stated how the organization had been impacted by the global staffing shortage as the rest of the industry has been. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
